==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|enm|Milener||native of Milan}}, irregular form of {{m|en|Milan}} + {{m|en|-er}}, from the purchase and importation of women's clothing from Milan.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|en|/ˈmɪlɪnɚ/}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-milliner.wav|Audio (Southern England)}}
* {{enPR|mĭ'lə-nər}}

